<title>CHINA: Dai-ichi Kangyo Bank opens in Pudong.</title>
<headline>Dai-ichi Kangyo Bank opens in Pudong.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Dai-ichi Kangyo Bank, one of nine foreign banks so far approved to do local Chinese yuan business, has opened a branch in Shanghai's Pudong development zone, the Shanghai Securities News said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>China's central bank has given approval to foreign banks to conduct local currency business on condition that they move their main Shanghai branch to Pudong, which the city wants to make into a major financial centre.</p>
</text>
